SUMMARY:OpenClawNet - Tools + Agent Workflows
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn this session we will transform o
 ur chatbot into an intelligent agent that can call tools to interact with 
 the outside world. We will build a tool framework with `ITool`\, `IToolReg
 istry`\, and `IToolExecutor` interfaces\, and implement production-ready t
 ools for file system access\, shell commands\, web fetching\, and task sch
 eduling — all with built-in security guardrails.\n\nAt the end we will h
 ave an agent that reasons through multi-step tasks on its own. Ask it to "
 Summarize my project's README" or "Check what's in my Downloads folder" 
 — it will break the problem into steps\, call the right tools\, and repo
 rt back.\n\n**Key Topics & Technologies:**\n\n* Agent orchestration and re
 asoning loops\n* Tool abstraction and design patterns\n* Security consider
 ations (path traversal\, command injection\, SSRF)\n* Tool UI and result s
 treaming\n* LLM function calling protocol\n* Dependency injection and serv
 ice registration\n* Structured logging and observability hooks\n\nPre-requ
 isites:\n\n* **Experience:** Intermediate C# and ASP.NET Core knowledge (n
 ot a .NET 101)\n* **Environment:** .NET 10 SDK\, VS Code + GitHub Copilot 
 (or Visual Studio)\, Docker (for Ollama)\n* **Optional:** Azure subscripti
 on (for Sessions 3–4\, but local development works fine throughout)\n* *
 *Mindset:** Curiosity about AI agents\, willingness to follow along live a
 nd ask questions
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3139
 46070/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260325T180311Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T180311Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
